        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$",
          "worked": "$\\tan^{-1}x$ is an odd function and the limits are symmetric about $0$, so\n$$\\int_{-5}^{5}\\tan^{-1}x\\,dx=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_{-3/4}^{3/4}\\cos^{-1}x\\,dx$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$",
          "worked": "$\\cos^{-1}x$ is neither odd nor even. Its graph has rotational symmetry about $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$. Over these symmetric limits, the area above $y=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ on the left equals the area below that line on the right. The integral therefore equals the area of a rectangle of height $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and width $\\frac{3}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_{-3/4}^{3/4}\\cos^{-1}x\\,dx&=\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\times\\frac{3}{2}\\\\&=\\frac{3\\pi}{4}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q12-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\int_{-2/3}^{2/3}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-x^2}}\\,dx$$",
