        "answer": {
          "short": "$18\\pi$",
          "worked": "$y=\\sqrt{36-x^2}$ describes the upper semicircle of radius $6$ and is non-negative on $[-6,6]$. Hence the integral is its area:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_{-6}^{6}\\sqrt{36-x^2}\\,dx&=\\frac12\\pi(6^2)\\\\&=18\\pi.\\end{aligned}$$",
